<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Braving the Weather</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;The war is over, and though no one expected adjustment to be easy, they also didn't anticipate just how much Etheria has been changed. As a creeping cold starts to settle over Brightmoon, Glimmer can't help the tension growing within her. She's okay now. Everyone is. They won. But for some reason, a mere gust of wind is still enough to send her running.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turns out, she's not the only one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Â &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Originally written for the Icebreaker Zine hosted by the SPOP Creative Flex discord server. Posted as part of the Thank You, She-Ra event.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>sakarrie</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Teen And Up Audiences</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra &amp; Glimmer (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Glimmer (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Gen</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>No Archive Warnings Apply</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Emotional Hurt/Comfort</rdf:li>
